course: dictionary
lesson: 6175
title: Minor: small, or not yet grown up
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Minor has more than one meaning, so context tells you which one to pick. «Pharmacists can give advice and medicines for many minor illnesses, and they send people to a doctor if something seems more serious.» The word «serious» is the clue. Minor here means small, or not very serious.
explain: Minor can also be a noun, a person. «A child flying alone, an unaccompanied minor, stays with the airline staff member who looks after them.» Here a minor is a young person who is not yet an adult. The sentence is about age, not size.
explain: Music uses minor too. A minor key often sounds sad, while a major key sounds happy. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: if small or not very serious still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: Minor is an adjective meaning small or not very important.
fact: «Minor injuries» are not serious, such as small cuts and scrapes that can be cleaned and covered with a plaster.
fact: As a noun, a minor is a person who is not yet an adult, under 18 in many countries.
fact: In music, a minor key often sounds sad, and a major key sounds happy.
fact: A «minor character» is a less important person in a story, not the main star.
exercise: «Urgent treatment centres deal with things like sprains, small cuts and minor burns.» What does minor mean in this sentence? | Very large and dangerous | *Small, not serious | Hidden under the ground | Happy and cheerful
exercise: In «an unaccompanied minor», what is a minor? | *A young person who is not yet an adult | A small tool for fixing things | A musical instrument | A part of a bus
exercise: Which kind of music key often sounds sad? | *Minor | Major | Fast | Loud
test: Which phrase means a problem that is small and not serious? | a giant problem | a major problem | *a minor problem | a huge problem
test: «Pharmacists can give advice for many minor illnesses.» What does minor mean here? | *Not very serious | Lost | Very old | Serious and dangerous
exam: In «a child flying alone, an unaccompanied minor, stays with the airline staff», what kind of word is minor? | A verb meaning to go down | *A noun meaning a person who is not yet an adult | An adverb meaning quickly | An adjective meaning small
